{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And look upon.</b> Parsed like ויחר לקין, and its meaning is like 'received,' and close to it is שעו מני, after the manner of the secret of the sacrifice. It is possible that fire descended and consumed the fat of Abel's offering but not Cain's offering. And in my opinion, a year is called תמימה ימים [complete days]; thus it is written ימים תהיה גאולתו (Leviticus 25:30), because the days return in length or shortness as they were at the beginning; likewise מימים ימימה [from days to days]. And שנתים ימים (Genesis 41:1) means two complete years in days; whereas if it were written שנתים alone, they might not be complete from day to day. Likewise עד חודש ימים (Numbers 11:20) — the month returns as it was. Therefore I said in my commentary on Daniel that ימים אלף מאתים ותשעים (Daniel 12:11) are days and not years, because they are in the number:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The comment contains a digression on the word 'days' that appears to have been appended to the Genesis 4:4 comment on וישע by thematic association; the transition is abrupt and the connection to the lemma is not explicit. Rendered as a single continuous passage as found in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:17.592109399Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}